  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Boeing is the federal vendor recorded on the page Boeing: Federal Contracts, Agencies & Awards for the period FY2026 to date. Boeing has total obligations of $5.9B across 490 awards, with an average award size of $12.1M and obligations up 35.7% year over year. Current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity. Historical obligations show variation by year, with FY21 at $7.3B, FY22 at $3.9B, FY23 at $3.3B, FY24 at $5B, FY25 at $4.4B, and FY26 at $5.9B. The Department of Defense is the top buying agency with $5.9B in obligations. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market by obligations at $5.9B, while several smaller NAICS markets register single-digit millions or less. This snapshot highlights concentration of Boeing federal work in defense and aircraft manufacturing for the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who buys the most from Boeing?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $5.9B for Boeing in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration recorded $0 in obligations for Boeing in the same period. These figures show Defense as the dominant buyer for Boeing so far this fiscal year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Boeing's top markets by obligations?",
        "body": "Aircraft Manufacturing accounts for $5.9B of Boeing obligations in FY2026 to date. Other notable markets are Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $63.4M and Computer Systems Design Services at $12.2M. Several markets range from $6.4M down to negative or zero values, reflecting much smaller or atypical recorded obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
